criteria.descriptionMarkdown:
The new group `tests/library_agnostic.rs` scans every non-test `src/**/*.rs` (files compiled only for tests, such as `src/app/test_support.rs`, and each file's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { ... }` are left out) and fails, listing `file:line: token`, for any word token (runs of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, compared case-insensitively with `-` and `_` equal) that is a library package name:

- exact names: `gpux`, `gpui`, the crates the CLI used to special-case (`branches`, `rclite`, `rxrust`, `indxdb`, `rexie`, `surrealdb`, `zune`), and RayX's library packages without a family prefix (`rayx_runtime`, `rayx_theme`, `rayx_macros`, `rayx_blocks`, `rayx_collab`, `rayx_lab`, `rayx_test_suite`, `rayx_code_theme_converter`, `rayx_mobile_smoke`);
- prefixes: `gpux_`, `gpui_`, `rayx_devkit`, `rayx_storage`, `rayx_components`, `rayx_reactive`, `rayx_signalr`, `dtcg_runtime`, `zune_`;
- the web page glue that belongs to apps (amendment 2): any token containing `htmlisland` or `html_island` (covers `HtmlIsland`, `__rayxHtmlIsland*` and the `rayx-html-island` switch), tokens starting with `__rayxthreaddiagnostics`, and the exact tokens `webgpu_status` and `wasm_thread_status`.

The bare word `rayx` is CLI vocabulary (binary, metadata namespaces, Lima VM) and is not denied; the removed `rayx` dependency special case is covered by ENTRY-1. An explicit allowlist holds `(file, token, reason)` entries for CLI vocabulary and non-package uses (for example `--branches` in a git command, prose naming the gpux and RayX work `rayx setup` prepares a machine for); every allowlist entry must still match something, so a stale entry fails too. A self-test runs the scanner on sample text: a planted `"gpux-fonts"` literal, a `gpui_mobile` identifier, `__rayxHtmlIslandEnabled` and `webgpu-status` are reported, the same text inside `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` is not, and an allowlisted token is not. The scan of the repository passes after the other requirements are implemented.

`docs/app-project.md` documents, with neutral example names:

- `entry_dependencies` (what it lists, how each entry is copied, how features enable optional ones, default none) in the `[package.metadata.rayx]` table, replacing the paragraph about `rayx` and `rayx_devkit`;
- `android_java_dirs` (who may declare it, relative paths, validation) and the Gradle property `rayxAndroidJavaDirs` an app's `build.gradle.kts` reads (split by `File.pathSeparator`) beside the other `-PrayxAndroid*` properties;
- that every generated entry crate starts from the project's `Cargo.lock`, and the generic `[patch]` rule (replacing "the IndexedDB storage crates");
- that fonts and other library assets come only through package assets (a `kind = "fonts"` asset package example);
- that `--android-devkit` needs the app's `devkit` feature;
- under "Files the app owns", `platform/web/index.html`: copied as `index.html`, the three placeholders `__RAYX_MODULE__`, `__RAYX_TITLE__`, `__RAYX_DIAGNOSTICS__` and what replaces them, the error for an unknown `__RAYX_*__` token, and the neutral fallback page shown in full as the starting template;
- the CLI vocabulary the guard allows (namespaces, `rayx.assets.toml`, `rayx_diagnostics`/`diagnostic_harness`, the `devkit` bridge with `RAYX_ANDROID_DEVKIT_PORT`, the default activity, the `RAYX_*` variables, the web page placeholders and the fallback's `data-rayx-wasm` marker, the `wasm_thread_entry_point` requirement);
- a "Migrating to rayx 1.4" section: what an app adds (`entry_dependencies`; including a fonts package id in an explicit `include`; reading `rayxAndroidJavaDirs` in Gradle), what a library adds (its package-asset declaration, `android_java_dirs`, a target dependency such as `branches/std` in the crate that needs it instead of relying on the CLI), what a workspace that relied on the gpux-checkout profile declares (`[workspace.metadata.rayx]` Android pins), that an app which relied on the generated diagnostics page adds `platform/web/index.html` with the three placeholders, and the behaviours that are gone.

The page names no gpux or RayX library package (it is library-agnostic like the code). Verified by the new group `tests/app_contract_docs.rs` (each key, property and section present; `gpux-checkout`, `rayx_devkit`, `gpux-fonts`, `IndexedDB`, `HtmlIsland`, `webgpu-status`, `zune` and `branches = ` absent).
